What the artifacts hold
=======================

The artifacts published on Maven Central — jtools-parent, jtools-support, jtools-server,
jtools-launcher, jtools-dist and jtools-web — hold the framework's own code and files
only: the Java libraries depend on nothing but the JDK, and jtools-web holds TypeScript
sources, no library of anyone else's.


The projects built with the framework
=====================================

A project's distributions, which jtools-parent builds from jtools-dist, bundle an Eclipse
Temurin (OpenJDK) runtime, licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2, with
the Classpath Exception, and its own licence and notices in their jre/legal/ directory;
and its page bundles the Angular libraries it depends on, whose licences its build writes
into static/licences/3rdpartylicenses.txt. Those are the project's to state in its own
NOTICE: the framework distributes neither.
